    },
    "index-1": {
      "html": "<p style=\"white-space:pre-wrap;\" class=\"sqsrte-large\" data-rte-preserve-empty=\"true\"><span class=\"sqsrte-text-color--custom\" style=\"color: #FE9295;\"><strong>A GRAFFITI STORY</strong></span></p><p class=\"\" style=\"white-space:pre-wrap;\" data-rte-preserve-empty=\"true\"><span class=\"sqsrte-text-color--white\"><strong>COMING 2/16/27</strong></span><span class=\"sqsrte-text-color--custom\" style=\"color: #FE9295;\"><br></span><span class=\"sqsrte-text-color--lightAccent\">Graphic Memoir (Abrams ComicArts 2023)</span><span class=\"sqsrte-text-color--white\"><br><br>An autobiographical YA graphic novel set in Seattle in the early 1990s. After a life-threatening neurological diagnosis and brain surgery leave him struggling to find his place, Josh discovers solace and purpose in Seattle’s vibrant underground graffiti scene. When he and a friend stumble upon a flyer for a legendary graffiti competition, they set out to make a name for themselves—risking arrest, family trust, and their futures in pursuit of artistic recognition. Fueled by creativity, friendship, and a diverse community of mentors and fellow artists, this true coming-of-age story offers a fresh, nuanced look at the often misunderstood world of graffiti while exploring resilience, identity, and the healing power of art.</span></p>",
      "slots": [
        {
          "key": "text_01",
          "start": 157,
          "end": 173,
          "kind": "text",
          "original": "A GRAFFITI STORY"
        },
