          "original": "Graphic Memoir (Abrams ComicArts 2023)"
        },
        {
          "key": "text_04",
          "start": 555,
          "end": 1283,
          "kind": "text",
          "original": "An autobiographical YA graphic novel set in Seattle in the early 1990s. After a life-threatening neurological diagnosis and brain surgery leave him struggling to find his place, Josh discovers solace and purpose in Seattle’s vibrant underground graffiti scene. When he and a friend stumble upon a flyer for a legendary graffiti competition, they set out to make a name for themselves—risking arrest, family trust, and their futures in pursuit of artistic recognition. Fueled by creativity, friendship, and a diverse community of mentors and fellow artists, this true coming-of-age story offers a fresh, nuanced look at the often misunderstood world of graffiti while exploring resilience, identity, and the healing power of art."
        }
      ],
