      "html": "<p class=\"\" style=\"white-space:pre-wrap;\" data-rte-preserve-empty=\"true\"><span class=\"sqsrte-text-color--custom\" style=\"color: #5DA1BA;\"><strong>INSPIRED BY A TRUE STORY</strong></span><br><span class=\"sqsrte-text-color--darkAccent\">(Abrams ComicArts 2023)<br><br>When Marco Calvo arrives at the Jewish Synagogue to attend his grandfather's funeral, he is caught off guard by something very unexpected. Among his close family and friends there are some people he doesn't recognize at all. Several Japanese American families have arrived and no one is quite sure why they are here. Who are these strangers that knew his grandfather so well? </span></p><p class=\"sqsrte-large\" style=\"white-space:pre-wrap;\" data-rte-preserve-empty=\"true\"><span class=\"sqsrte-text-color--custom\" style=\"color: #5DA1BA;\"><strong>AWARDS &amp; HONORS</strong></span></p><p class=\"sqsrte-small\" style=\"white-space:pre-wrap;\" data-rte-preserve-empty=\"true\"><span class=\"sqsrte-text-color--darkAccent\"><strong>2024 </strong>Washington State Book Award  |  <strong>FINALIST<br>2024</strong>National EGLA AWARD |  Best YA Non-Fiction Graphic Novel <strong>WINNER<br>2024</strong>National Jewish Book Award  |  <strong>FINALIST<br>2024 </strong>American Library Association |Sophie Brody Medal<strong> HONOREE<br>2024</strong> KCLS Literary Lions  | <strong> HONOR<br>2024</strong>Anti-Defamation League | <strong>Books Matter Collection<br>2024</strong>Jewish Comic Experience | Combating Prejudice <strong>AWARD<br>2025 </strong>Tacoma Public LIbrary  |  <strong>Tacoma Reads Book of 2025</strong><br><strong>2026 </strong>King County Library  | <strong>Redmond Reads Book of 2026</strong></span></p>",
